{"name":"Midsummer Twilight","hex":"#b1a4b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midsummer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The period around the summer solstice; around June 21st in the northern hemisphere.","The first day of summer."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or occurring in the middle of summer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midsummer"},{"term":"twilight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soft light in the sky seen before the rising and (especially) after the setting of the sun, occasioned by the illumination of the earth’s atmosphere by the direct rays of the sun and their reflection on the earth.","The time when said light is visible; the period between daylight and darkness."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to or resembling twilight; faintly illuminated; obscure.","Synonym of mesopelagic (“Describing the pelagic zone of the ocean between the photic epipelagic and the aphotic bathypelagic zones, characterized by very minimal light.”)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twilight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midsummer","blocks":[{"text":"Midsummer or Midsommar is a celebration of the season of summer, taking place on or near the date of the summer solstice in the Northern Hemisphere, the longest day of the year. The name midsummer mainly refers to summer solstice festivals of European origin. These cultures traditionally regard it as the middle of summer, with the season beginning on May Day. Although the summer solstice falls on 20, 21 or 22 June in the Northern Hemisphere, it was traditionally reckoned to fall on 23–24 June in much of Europe. These dates were Christianized as Saint John's Eve and Saint John's Day. It is usually celebrated with outdoor gatherings that include bonfires, maypole dancing and feasting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Mittsommerfest_in_Norwegen%2C_Insel_Tysnes_IMG_4425WI.jpg/330px-Mittsommerfest_in_Norwegen%2C_Insel_Tysnes_IMG_4425WI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midsummer","wikidata":"Q154502"},{"title":"Twilight","blocks":[{"text":"Twilight is daylight illumination produced by diffuse sky radiation when the Sun is below the horizon as sunlight from the upper atmosphere is scattered in a way that illuminates both the Earth's lower atmosphere and also the Earth's surface. Twilight also may be any period when this illumination occurs, including dawn and dusk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Twilight_description_full_day.svg/330px-Twilight_description_full_day.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilight","wikidata":"Q164160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg/500px-Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg/500px-Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Midsummer Eve Bonfire by Norwegian artist Nikolai Astrup (c.1915)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG/500px-KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG/500px-KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A maypole at Midsummer near the Kastelholm Castle in Sund, Åland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKastelholmMidso